From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000004 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Tue, 4 Nov 2026 21:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shusky halium.config: drop CFI_PERMISSIVE when CFI is off

With CONFIG_CFI_CLANG disabled (aosp/0017), CFI_PERMISSIVE no longer
exists in Kconfig and kleaf's fragment validation fails the build
("actual '', expected CONFIG_CFI_PERMISSIVE=y"). Turn it off here.

---
 google/shusky/halium.config | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/google/shusky/halium.config b/google/shusky/halium.config
index 31ce547e..666666666666 100644
--- a/google/shusky/halium.config
+++ b/google/shusky/halium.config
@@ -25,2 +25,2 @@
 CONFIG_SQUASHFS_ZSTD=y
-CONFIG_CFI_PERMISSIVE=y
+# CONFIG_CFI_PERMISSIVE is not set
